// Sign in with Google and Sign in with Apple on iOS, and the entitlements the
// app is signed with. The sign-in settings stay empty or off in Git and inert
// until Ismail sets them; the Runner's "Check sign-in settings" build phase
// (ios/scripts/check_social_sign_in.sh) fails a build whose build defines
// disagree with them.
//
// GOOGLE_IOS_CLIENT_PREFIX  the iOS OAuth client id without its
//                           ".apps.googleusercontent.com" ending, such as
//                           1234567890-abcdef. The URL scheme Google returns
//                           to (com.googleusercontent.apps.<prefix>) is made
//                           from it, and the GOOGLE_IOS_CLIENT_ID define must
//                           be <prefix>.apps.googleusercontent.com.
//
// APPLE_SIGN_IN_CAPABILITY  YES once the App ID has the Sign in with Apple
//                           capability; NO, the app is signed without it.
//                           Required YES when the build defines
//                           APPLE_SIGN_IN_ENABLED=true.
GOOGLE_IOS_CLIENT_PREFIX =
APPLE_SIGN_IN_CAPABILITY = NO

// The Runner's CODE_SIGN_ENTITLEMENTS. Push notifications (aps-environment)
// are in both files, so every signed build can receive them; only Sign in
// with Apple is switched. "development" is what Xcode writes: signing for
// the App Store takes the production value from the distribution profile.
RUNNER_ENTITLEMENTS_NO = Runner/Runner.entitlements
RUNNER_ENTITLEMENTS_YES = Runner/RunnerAppleSignIn.entitlements
RUNNER_ENTITLEMENTS = $(RUNNER_ENTITLEMENTS_$(APPLE_SIGN_IN_CAPABILITY))
